, our tour coordinator. He also helped in arranging our water sports activities, which were truly amazing. We had a great time, and my friend and I will definitely use these services again in the future and recommend them to others. Thank you for a great experience.","link":"https://www.google.com/maps/reviews/data=!4m8!14m7!1m6!2m5!1sCi9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2tSdE1sTjNTbVJaUlhZM1ZERkpVMFZOYUVsWmFWRRAB!2m1!1s0x0:0xd472e9b000192411!3m1!1s2@1:CAIQACodChtycF9oOkRtMlN3SmRZRXY3VDFJU0VNaElZaVE%7C%7C?hl=en-GB","date":"7 months ago","date_iso8601":"2026-02-15T17:03:58+00:00"},{"username":"Arjun Naik","rating":1,"contributor_id":"117826685860329989038","user_review_count":15,"user_photo_count":8,"user_thumbnail":"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUaPmbtc191GHSHvDkDrETXvgNTWlsWfDV-1xlIW7LWPrItGyIVrA=s120-c-rp-mo-ba12-br100","description":"❌❌❌I had a very disappointing experience with the watersports here, and honestly, it felt like a complete scam. They charged ₹1500 for a package of 5 activities, but none of them were worth the money.\n\nParasailing was barely 45 seconds, and they didn’t even take us properly high into the sky. It felt rushed and underwhelming. The jet ski ride was even worse — they don’t allow you to ride it yourself unless you pay an extra ₹300. Otherwise, you just sit there while someone else controls it, which completely defeats the experience.\n\nThe same issue applies to banana ride, bumper ride, and other activities. Everything is extremely short, and at every step, they keep asking for extra money if you want to go farther, ride yourself, or get a better experience. It feels like they deliberately give a poor basic service just to push you into paying more.\n\nOverall, it’s not worth the money at all and leaves you feeling cheated rather than excited.\n\nI strongly recommend avoiding this place. Instead, go for watersports at Mobor Beach in South Goa — they offer a much better, fair, and enjoyable experience without these hidden charges and 